&lt;p&gt;At PandaDoc, we&#39;re building the future of documents. Our platform helps teams create, send, track, and e-sign proposals, contracts, and other documents, making our clients&#39; lives more efficient and collaborative. We&#39;re a fast-growing company with a global reach, used by people around the world, from small businesses to large enterprises. In 2024, we reached a major milestone: over $100 million in annual recurring revenue. We&#39;re constantly innovating and releasing new features to meet the evolving needs of our customers, all while focusing on stability, quality, and performance.&lt;br&gt;Our Engineering team is a diverse and talented group of around 250 individuals, passionate about building a world-class product. While this is a fully remote position, we&#39;d love for you to visit our vibrant offices in Warsaw, Lisbon, or Kyiv whenever you&#39;d like to connect with colleagues in person.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Python Engineer to join our Content engineering team&lt;/strong&gt;, responsible for one of the most complex and impactful areas of the PandaDoc platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We own the content model, the editor backend, data persistence, and the real-time collaboration infrastructure that allows multiple users to edit a document simultaneously with consistency and reliability. Our backend processes a continuous stream of events from the frontend, translating user interactions into consistent, durable state across a distributed fleet of services and a high volume of concurrent sessions.&lt;br&gt;We ship product features and maintain the systems that underpin them. Product mindset and operational excellence are not in tension here: we expect engineers who care equally about moving the product forward for customers and about the long-term health and reliability of what they build.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve the backend systems that power real-time collaborative document editing for tens of thousands of concurrent users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the content model and data persistence layer: schema design, migrations, compatibility, and long-term maintainability as the product grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain event-driven pipelines (Kafka, NATS) that process high volumes of frontend interactions and keep document state consistent across services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the reliability, observability, and operational excellence of a large fleet of Python microservices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship product features end-to-end, from backend architecture to production monitoring, and care about how they behave after they ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our growing investment in AI-powered capabilities, including agentic document workflows&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core language:&lt;/strong&gt; Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relational + caching:&lt;/strong&gt; PostgreSQL, Redis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Messaging &amp;amp; events:&lt;/strong&gt; Kafka, NATS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Async programming:&lt;/strong&gt; AsyncIO throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Docker, Kubernetes, AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Grafana stack (Loki, Tempo, Mimir)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
